    "Question #: 2": {
      "Title": "Exam AZ-200 topic 1 question 8 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Each year, a company consolidates manufacturing data for a year and stores the data in a single blob within a Blob container. Data from previous years is stored in the same storage account in the same container."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The company has a General Purpose v2 (GPv2) Azure Storage account with a Blob container named Compliance-data. Data from previous years is retained for compliance reasons but it is infrequently accesses."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The current solution is becoming costly. You observe that users accidentally modify compliance data."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You need to reduce costs and preserve the compliance data."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "What should you do?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. In the Azure Portal, go to configuration settings of each blob in the Compliance-data container and set Access tier to Archive."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. Set up another GPv2 storage account and copy data to the new storage account."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. In the Azure Portal, go to configuration settings for each blob in the Compliance-data container and set the Access tier to Cool."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. Configure another GPv2 cold storage account and copy data to the new storage account."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: C \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Cool storage is optimized for storing data that is infrequently accessed and stored for at least 30 days."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Incorrect Answers:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A: Archive storage is optimized for storing data that is rarely accessed and stored for at least 180 days with flexible latency requirements (on the order of hours)."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "References:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "https://docs.microsoft.com/en-in/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blob-storage-tiers"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Cool storage is optimized for storing data that is infrequently accessed and stored for at least 30 days."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Incorrect Answers:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A: Archive storage is optimized for storing data that is rarely accessed and stored for at least 180 days with flexible latency requirements (on the order of hours)."
